  nonce: 92b2  # 92b2
  message: "DEPENDENCY NOTE: WI-toruz carries a re-evaluation trigger keyed on THIS item's ruling. WI-toruz rules call_construct=constructor CANONICAL on instantiates edges, and its stated reason is that the value is the only cross-language invariant for object creation that survives the edge_type disagreement documented here. If this item is ruled such that ONE edge_type carries all object creation across every language, then constructor becomes derivable from edge_type and WI-toruz's Keep verdict flips to a fold. Whoever rules this item should re-read WI-toruz before closing."  # 92b2
- op: discuss  # 5900
  at: '2026-08-20T22:22:16Z'  # 5900
  by: agent  # 5900
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5900
  clock: 3  # 5900
  nonce: '5900'  # 5900
  message: "HUMAN RULING (2026-08-20 interview): OPTION A, sequenced third behind the taint fix. The owner approved the proposed order verbatim -- (1) confirm the Popen repro, (2) file and fix the taint call-family gap, (3) then harmonize Ruby under option A. WHAT OPTION A IS: ruby emits edge_type=instantiates for object creation, keeping its existing dst (Klass#initialize, the initializer symbol). Ruby's dst choice is NOT changing -- it was already correct, and WI-fagit (PR #689) independently converged csharp onto the same choice on bakeoff evidence, landing instantiates on the CONSTRUCTOR node rather than the class because the class node conflates 'referenced as a type' with 'instantiated' and broke reverse-slice. So only the LABEL moves. WHY THE SEQUENCING IS LOAD-BEARING AND NOT A PREFERENCE: TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES excludes instantiates, so moving ruby's constructor edges into that edge type BEFORE the taint fix would make ruby object creation taint-invisible -- widening the INV-lalad blind spot rather than paying a one-off cost. INV-lalad must land first; option A is then cost-free. OPTIONS REJECTED, recorded so this is not re-litigated: (B) the 8 analyzers switch to calls -- rejected, contradicts WI-fagit's motivation and discards the one label that makes 'who constructs this' queryable; (C) emit both edges -- rejected for edge-count inflation at every construction site plus edge_key/dedup consequences; (D) keep and document the synonym set per the WI-moliz keep-distinct precedent -- rejected because INV-nosoz is the live demonstration of where leaving enumeration to consumers ends (five disagreeing copies of one set)."  # 5900
