- op: discuss  # f190
  at: '2026-08-21T02:20:46Z'  # f190
  by: agent  # f190
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f190
  clock: 5  # f190
  nonce: f190  # f190
  message: "CLOSED, with behavioral evidence on the MERGED tree (d8d415dd0d) -- and with one claim of mine REFUTED by the measurement. Do not read this as an unqualified win.\n\nWHAT THE ITEM ASKED, AND WHETHER IT HOLDS. The statement was: one source-language construct (object creation) must produce one relationship label across languages, so a consumer can enumerate every object creation with a single edge_type query. SATISFIED, demonstrated end-to-end through the real survey CLI on a two-language fixture (ruby + python). The single query type == instantiates now returns BOTH: ruby Factory#build -> Widget#initialize, python build -> Gadget. Languages returned: [python, ruby]. Before the fix that query returned python only and silently omitted all of ruby.\n\nTHE REACHABILITY HALF: MECHANISM PROVED, CORPUS EFFECT ZERO. On real survey output from a ruby cascade fixture, seeding Factory#build: OLD set {calls,dispatches_to,wraps} reaches only Factory#build; NEW set also reaches Widget#initialize, Widget#normalize, Widget#audit. Three symbols recovered, two of them purely transitive -- so the constructor-and-downstream cascade is real where it applies.\n\nBUT on hypergumbo own corpus the delta is EXACTLY ZERO, and I measured it rather than assuming. Method (thanks to the owner for the instrument): ephemeral clone at /tmp/hg-old rewound to 9db326c416, run via PYTHONPATH shadowing so the console script loads the OLD cli.py, both runs fed the SAME fixed 44,842-node survey. Instrument verified before trusting it -- the old process resolves to /tmp/hg-old/...cli.py and reports the literal {calls, dispatches_to, wraps}. Result, old vs new: total_production_functions 5201/5201, seed_count 1279/1279, reachable_functions 2843/2843, dead_candidates 2152/2152, dead_percent 41.4/41.4. Byte-identical output.\n\nWHY ZERO, MEASURED NOT GUESSED. All 11,260 instantiates edges in that graph point at kind=class (8,919) or external_symbol (2,341). ZERO point at a callable. The 524 distinct class nodes they target have only contains (2,814), extends (190) and decorated_by (5) leaving them -- none traversable by the reachability BFS. So construction reaches a class node, the class node is not a production function, and it leads nowhere. Separately: all 73 python __init__ symbols in the graph have contains as their ONLY incoming edge type -- zero calls, zero instantiates in 157,468 edges -- and 0 of the 2,152 dead candidates are __init__.\n\nTHE CLAIM OF MINE THIS REFUTES. My commit message says the constructor AND everything transitively downstream of it were false dead code, for all nine emitting languages. That is OVERSTATED. The mechanism was broken for all nine, but the consequence only bites where the dst is a CALLABLE -- ruby now, and csharp post-WI-fagit. Where the dst is the CLASS (python: 100% of hypergumbo own instantiates edges) the fix is INERT, because class-to-method is contains, which confers no reachability and correctly so -- containing is not calling. The fix is right and the hole was real; its realized value is conditional on the dst choice, and I should have measured that before writing the stronger sentence.\n\nFOLLOW-UP FILED for the python dst gap."  # f190
